00:14:40,650 --> 00:14:42,650
meaning that they start with a slash,

152
00:14:42,650 --> 00:14:46,680
and they go all the way down in the hierarchy.

153
00:14:46,680 --> 00:14:52,680
They can be relative to a particular, whatever your current directory is,

154
00:14:52,680 --> 00:14:57,680
where, and they can also be relative to a user,

155
00:14:57,680 --> 00:15:03,100
if you use the tilda slash,

156
00:15:03,100 --> 00:15:08,100
then that's sort of a shortcut in this path name to get to particular users.

157
00:15:08,100 --> 00:15:12,420
users. So a path name can be any of those forms when you open it.

